783
00:35:25.960 --> 00:35:26.760
Tinks club.
Tinks夜店。

784
00:35:26.760 --> 00:35:29.680
Michael would have had a talking head here that got cut.
迈克尔本来有个单人访谈镜头，但被剪掉了。

785
00:35:29.680 --> 00:35:33.460
It was in the shooting draft where he says, I know, Tinks.
在拍摄剧本里他说，我知道Tinks。

786
00:35:33.500 --> 00:35:35.380
I go there every Friday night.
我每周五晚上都去那儿。

787
00:35:35.660 --> 00:35:37.340
Well, I wait in line there.
好吧，我是在那儿排队。

788
00:35:37.540 --> 00:35:39.280
You meet a lot of fun people online.
你在网上能遇到很多有趣的人。

789
00:35:39.520 --> 00:35:41.760
I've never been inside, but I wouldn't want...
我从来没进去过，但我也不想……

790
00:35:41.760 --> 00:35:42.500
Online or in line?
是在网上还是排队？

791
00:35:42.720 --> 00:35:42.860
Sorry.
抱歉。

792
00:35:42.960 --> 00:35:43.320
Online.
网上。

793
00:35:43.880 --> 00:35:44.060
Okay.
好的。

794
00:35:44.160 --> 00:35:44.460
Sorry.
抱歉。

795
00:35:44.640 --> 00:35:44.840
Sorry.
抱歉。

796
00:35:44.960 --> 00:35:45.240
Go ahead.
你继续。

797
00:35:45.320 --> 00:35:45.520
Okay.
好的。

798
00:35:45.780 --> 00:35:47.720
You meet a lot of fun people online.
你在排队时能遇到很多有趣的人。

799
00:35:48.360 --> 00:35:50.860
I've never been inside, but I wouldn't want to.
我从来没进去过，但我也不想进去。

800
00:35:51.120 --> 00:35:52.280
It's for people half my age.
那是给只有我一半大的人去的。

801
00:35:52.660 --> 00:35:55.020
Part of me just wants to give up online dating altogether.
我有一部分心思真的想彻底放弃网上约会了。

802
00:35:55.020 --> 00:35:57.780
I really hate when Friday night rolls around.
我真的很讨厌周五晚上到来的时候。

803
00:35:58.000 --> 00:35:58.460
Wait.
等等。

804
00:35:58.800 --> 00:36:00.060
There's so much there.
那里面信息量好大。

805
00:36:00.300 --> 00:36:05.060
He thinks online dating is you go and stand in a long line at a nightclub.
他以为网上约会就是去夜店排长队。

806
00:36:05.300 --> 00:36:06.280
Oh my gosh.
天哪。

807
00:36:07.380 --> 00:36:08.300
Come on.
得了吧。

808
00:36:08.440 --> 00:36:09.560
Isn't that so good?
这难道不好吗？

809
00:36:10.080 --> 00:36:11.480
That is so good.
这太棒了。

810
00:36:11.900 --> 00:36:18.100
Between Maury talking about Tinks and me reading about this deleted talking head where Michael talks about Tinks,
莫里在聊Tinks，而我读到了一段被删减的访谈，迈克尔在里面提到了Tinks，

811
00:36:18.100 --> 00:36:21.900
I had to know, is Tinks a real place?
我必须得弄清楚，Tinks是个真实存在的地方吗？

812
00:36:22.280 --> 00:36:23.940
And by the way, it is.
顺便说一句，确实是。

813
00:36:24.080 --> 00:36:25.660
It was a total hotspot, Jenna.
它曾经是个超级热门的地方，珍娜。

814
00:36:26.360 --> 00:36:27.400
But here's the thing.
但重点是。

815
00:36:27.560 --> 00:36:33.960
While I was researching that, I got so fascinated with the history of the building that Tinks was in.
我在研究这个的时候，对Tinks所在那栋建筑的历史着了迷。

816
00:36:34.100 --> 00:36:35.260
I have to share about it.
我一定要分享一下。

817
00:36:35.500 --> 00:36:36.520
I took a picture.
我拍了张照片。

818
00:36:36.680 --> 00:36:37.640
I'll put it in stories.
我会发到快拍里。

819
00:36:38.280 --> 00:36:39.780
Look at this place, Jenna.
看看这个地方，珍娜。

820
00:36:40.400 --> 00:36:41.540
Right there in the middle.
就在正中间。

821
00:36:41.740 --> 00:36:43.320
That's where Tinks would have been.
那就是Tinks曾经所在的位置。

822
00:36:43.500 --> 00:36:45.080
This looks very...
这看起来非常……

823
00:36:45.080 --> 00:36:47.080
I feel like I'm looking at a picture of London.
我觉得我像是在看一张伦敦的照片。

824
00:36:47.080 --> 00:36:47.660
I know.
我知道。

825
00:36:47.760 --> 00:36:48.560
It looks old, right?
看起来很古老，对吧？

826
00:36:48.560 --> 00:36:50.480
It looks old English to me.
我觉得看起来很有英伦古风。

827
00:36:50.620 --> 00:36:56.680
I found a great article on the Scranton Times Tributes website written by Brian Fulton.
我在《斯克兰顿时报》的致敬网站上找到了一篇布莱恩·富尔顿写的很棒的文章。

828
00:36:56.940 --> 00:36:59.980
Brian, I loved all your info.
布莱恩，我超爱你的这些资料。

829
00:37:00.280 --> 00:37:01.480
Here's some of it, okay?
我摘录了一些，好吗？

830
00:37:01.940 --> 00:37:06.580
The location of Tinks is 519 Linden Street in Scranton.
Tinks的位置在斯克兰顿的林登街519号。

831
00:37:06.700 --> 00:37:09.460
It was constructed in 1909.
它建于1909年。

832
00:37:09.700 --> 00:37:10.600
It looks old!
看起来确实老！

833
00:37:10.800 --> 00:37:11.360
I know!
我知道！

834
00:37:11.560 --> 00:37:20.340
It was the Courthouse Square Garage, which sold Studebakers and EFM automobiles over the years.
它曾经是法院广场车库，多年来销售过斯图贝克和EFM汽车。

835
00:37:20.500 --> 00:37:23.240
It would be a series of dealerships.
它后来成了多家经销商的所在地。

836
00:37:23.320 --> 00:37:26.700
It went on to be an electric appliance store, sporting goods stores.
之后又变成了电器商店和体育用品商店。

837
00:37:27.000 --> 00:37:30.560
In the mid-20s, it became the Scranton Recreation.
20世纪20年代中期，它变成了斯克兰顿娱乐中心。

838
00:37:30.560 --> 00:37:34.080
It offered a bowling alley, a billiard room on the third floor.
它提供保龄球馆，三楼还有台球室。

839
00:37:34.720 --> 00:37:40.520
30 years later, in the 50s, Rene Dress operated on the building's second floor.
30年后，也就是50年代，勒内服装店在二楼经营。

840
00:37:41.140 --> 00:37:46.880
Then the Linden Dress Corporation bought the whole building, expanding to the third floor
后来林登服装公司买下了整栋楼，扩展到了三楼，

841
00:37:46.880 --> 00:37:50.340
with retail and dining establishments on the ground floor.
一楼则开设了零售店和餐饮场所。

842
00:37:51.420 --> 00:37:57.420
In 1988, it was going to have an open-air cafe, a new banquet hall that could seat 150,
1988年，这里计划开设一家露天咖啡馆，一个能容纳150人的新宴会厅，

843
00:37:57.740 --> 00:38:00.220
and the creation of a dinner theater.
还要创建一个晚餐剧场。

844
00:38:00.560 --> 00:38:01.160
Oh!
哦！

845
00:38:01.380 --> 00:38:01.880
Yes!
没错！

846
00:38:02.140 --> 00:38:08.220
The first dinner theater production to take place was called Nifty 50s, a musical review.
第一部在晚餐剧场上演的作品叫《俏丽50年代》，是一场音乐评论秀。

847
00:38:08.500 --> 00:38:12.280
Then they started offering live music on Tuesdays and Sundays.
后来他们开始在周二和周日提供现场音乐表演。

848
00:38:12.280 --> 00:38:22.540
Anyways, in 1994, they sold Tinks to John Paul and Angela Cooper, operators of Cooper's Seafood
总之，1994年，他们把Tinks卖给了约翰·保罗和安吉拉·库珀，他们是斯克兰顿库珀海鲜

849
00:38:22.540 --> 00:38:23.380
House in Scranton.
餐厅的经营者。

850
00:38:23.720 --> 00:38:24.260
Oh!
哦！

851
00:38:24.620 --> 00:38:28.160
The venue remained a popular night spot in Scranton.
这个场地一直是斯克兰顿的热门夜店。

852
00:38:28.400 --> 00:38:31.260
It was a hub for live music for years.
多年来，它一直是现场音乐的中心。

853
00:38:31.260 --> 00:38:38.360
All these amazing bands would come through, and then in the fall of 2015, it became Levels
所有这些很棒的乐队都会来这里演出，后来在2015年秋天，它变成了Levels

854
00:38:38.360 --> 00:38:41.660
on Linden, and they closed March of this year.
on Linden，并在今年三月关门了。

855
00:38:41.840 --> 00:38:46.160
But it started out as a car garage selling Studebakers.
但它最初是一家卖斯图贝克汽车的车库。

856
00:38:46.160 --> 00:38:50.520
I'll tell you that I got really stopped.
我得告诉你，我真的被卡住了。

857
00:38:50.680 --> 00:38:53.840
You know when someone's telling you a story, and you hear a part of that story, and then
你知道当有人在给你讲故事时，你听到故事的一部分，然后

858
00:38:53.840 --> 00:38:56.120
your brain kind of goes in another place?
你的大脑就会飘到别的地方去了吗？

859
00:38:57.200 --> 00:39:00.940
When you said Nifty 50s musical review...
当你提到“五十年代风情”音乐评论时……

860
00:39:00.940 --> 00:39:02.680
You could only think of Andy Bernard.
你只能想到安迪·伯纳德。

861
00:39:03.300 --> 00:39:12.460
No, I could only think of you and I doing the Nifty 50s dinner theater musical review,
不，我只能想到你和我一起做“五十年代风情”晚餐剧场音乐评论，

862
00:39:12.460 --> 00:39:13.680
and what that might be.
那会是什么样子。

863
00:39:13.800 --> 00:39:18.340
And I'm going to be honest with you, I went off on that for a while in my head.
老实说，我在脑子里想了好一会儿。

864
00:39:18.720 --> 00:39:22.920
But I made it back to hear that the Cooper's people bought it.
但我回过神来，听到库珀家的人把它买下来了。

865
00:39:23.100 --> 00:39:26.640
And then it was a series of nightclubs, and it closed this year.
后来它成了一系列夜总会，今年关门了。

866
00:39:26.820 --> 00:39:27.240
Okay.
好吧。

867
00:39:27.240 --> 00:39:28.960
So I guess it's available.
所以我猜它现在空着呢。

868
00:39:29.000 --> 00:39:30.220
It's available!
它空着呢！

869
00:39:30.720 --> 00:39:33.460
For Angela and Jenna's musical theater review!
正好给安吉拉和珍娜做音乐剧评论！

870
00:39:34.140 --> 00:39:35.340
I'm just saying.
我只是随口一说。

871
00:39:35.740 --> 00:39:36.840
Oh my gosh.
天哪。

872
00:39:37.180 --> 00:39:38.440
Nifty 50s.
五十年代风情。

873
00:39:38.580 --> 00:39:40.040
Nifty 50s!
五十年代风情！

874
00:39:40.080 --> 00:39:43.160
I mean, has anything been more made for us?
我是说，还有什么比这更适合我们的吗？

875
00:39:43.280 --> 00:39:44.680
Well, I just turned 50.
嗯，我刚满50岁。

876
00:39:44.880 --> 00:39:47.520
I think we wait for you to turn 50 in a few years.
我想我们得等你几年后满50岁再说。

877
00:39:47.620 --> 00:39:47.800
Yeah.
是啊。

878
00:39:47.940 --> 00:39:49.940
And then we go do the Nifty 50s.
然后我们就去搞那个“五十年代风情”。

879
00:39:50.300 --> 00:39:50.820
Yes!
太棒了！

880
00:39:51.680 --> 00:39:54.440
That's all I've been thinking about since you said it.
自从你说了之后，我就一直在想这件事。

881
00:39:54.440 --> 00:39:57.480
I love the history of old buildings.
我喜欢老建筑的历史。

882
00:39:57.660 --> 00:39:58.960
I absolutely love it.
我非常喜欢。

883
00:39:59.120 --> 00:40:03.140
I love to think about the different people that came in and out of that space.
我喜欢想象那些进出过这个空间的不同的人。

884
00:40:03.300 --> 00:40:03.480
Yeah.
是啊。

885
00:40:03.760 --> 00:40:08.880
And the memories that were made, whether you were buying your very first car and it was
还有那些留下的回忆，无论你是买了你的第一辆车，而且是

886
00:40:08.880 --> 00:40:12.040
a Studebaker, or you were doing dinner theater.
一辆斯图贝克，还是你在那里演晚餐剧场。

887
00:40:12.340 --> 00:40:14.180
Or you were getting a dress made.
或者你在那里定做了一件礼服。

888
00:40:14.480 --> 00:40:15.000
Yes!
没错！

889
00:40:15.000 --> 00:40:21.040
Or you were meeting your lady love for a rendezvous, Stanley.
或者你在那里和你的爱人幽会，斯坦利。

890
00:40:22.000 --> 00:40:28.200
Well, when Stanley leaves the office, Michael is so excited to share what he thinks he's
嗯，当斯坦利离开办公室时，迈克尔非常兴奋地分享他认为自己

891
00:40:28.200 --> 00:40:31.000
learned, which is that Stanley is having a midlife crisis.
了解到的情况，那就是斯坦利正在经历中年危机。

892
00:40:31.340 --> 00:40:31.600
Yeah.
是啊。

893
00:40:31.820 --> 00:40:33.260
Because he was out at this club.
因为他当时在那家俱乐部。

894
00:40:33.760 --> 00:40:36.160
But Dwight says, no.
但德怀特说，不。

895
00:40:36.560 --> 00:40:38.800
Stanley is way past the middle of his life.
斯坦利早就过了中年了。

896
00:40:38.800 --> 00:40:44.640
And Phyllis is like, Michael, what you're saying isn't true because Terry is out of
菲利斯说，迈克尔，你说的不是真的，因为特里出

897
00:40:44.640 --> 00:40:46.180
town and Stanley hates crowds.
城了，而且斯坦利讨厌人群。

898
00:40:46.360 --> 00:40:47.000
He hates music.
他讨厌音乐。

899
00:40:47.240 --> 00:40:48.180
He hates kids.
他讨厌小孩。

900
00:40:48.400 --> 00:40:49.740
You should check your facts.
你应该核实一下你的事实。

901
00:40:49.900 --> 00:40:51.160
We got some Phyllis sass.
菲利斯开始耍嘴皮子了。

902
00:40:51.420 --> 00:40:53.620
Well, Michael's going to march up to the interns.
迈克尔打算去找实习生们。

903
00:40:53.900 --> 00:40:54.940
He's fired up.
他现在斗志昂扬。

904
00:40:55.560 --> 00:41:00.200
Jenna, I want you to know this scene started differently in the shooting draft.
珍娜，我想让你知道，这场戏在拍摄剧本里原本不是这样开头的。

905
00:41:00.360 --> 00:41:00.520
Oh.
噢。

906
00:41:00.740 --> 00:41:07.520
Michael is still going to march up, but the interns are gossiping as he arrives.
迈克尔还是会走过去，但实习生们在他到达时正在闲聊。

907
00:41:08.140 --> 00:41:08.760
Oh.
噢。

908
00:41:09.080 --> 00:41:09.580
Uh-huh.
嗯哼。

909
00:41:09.980 --> 00:41:14.740
It says interior break room, Maury, Eric, and Maria, because that's what she was called
剧本上写着内景休息室，莫里、埃里克和玛丽亚——因为她在拍摄剧本里叫这个名字——

910
00:41:14.740 --> 00:41:20.760
in the shooting draft, are in an assembly line style, unstapling and collating and stapling.
他们像流水线一样，在拆订书钉、整理文件，然后再装订。

911
00:41:21.220 --> 00:41:22.600
Michael barges in.
迈克尔闯了进来。

912
00:41:23.200 --> 00:41:26.240
Maury says, you see what Erin's wearing today?
莫里说，你看到艾琳今天穿什么了吗？

913
00:41:26.700 --> 00:41:29.520
Eric, I'm more of a Pam kind of guy.
埃里克说，我更喜欢帕姆那种类型的。

914
00:41:30.200 --> 00:41:34.900
Maria, the warehouse guys were saying she's dated like everyone in the office.
玛丽亚说，仓库的人都在说她跟办公室里的每个人都约会过。

915
00:41:35.240 --> 00:41:36.520
Oh my gosh!
天哪！

916
00:41:37.520 --> 00:41:43.120
And then at this moment, Michael says, you stupid son of a bitch, you set me up.
然后就在这时，迈克尔说，你这蠢货，你陷害我。

917
00:41:44.540 --> 00:41:54.360
Well, this is when it finally occurs to Michael after much explanation that perhaps Stanley was
好吧，这是在经过多次解释后，迈克尔终于意识到斯坦利可能

918
00:41:54.360 --> 00:41:56.280
there with someone other than his wife.
是和除了他妻子以外的人在一起。

919
00:41:56.280 --> 00:42:00.740
The amount of time it takes Michael to clue in on something.
迈克尔反应过来一件事所花的时间。

920
00:42:00.860 --> 00:42:01.520
Oh my gosh.
天哪。

921
00:42:01.640 --> 00:42:02.840
Is one of my favorite things.
是我最喜欢的事情之一。

922
00:42:03.060 --> 00:42:03.220
Yeah.
是啊。

923
00:42:03.780 --> 00:42:08.260
Well, now Michael really has some gossip and he is so excited to share it.
现在迈克尔真的掌握了一些八卦，他兴奋得不得了，迫不及待想分享。

924
00:42:08.400 --> 00:42:15.060
He does not at all understand the gravity of what he's sharing and the damage it could do to multiple lives.
他完全不明白他所分享的内容有多严重，以及这会对多个人的生活造成多大的伤害。

925
00:42:15.260 --> 00:42:17.720
He's just giddy to have a little tidbit of info.
他只是因为掌握了一点小道消息而感到飘飘然。

926
00:42:17.720 --> 00:42:22.600
He runs over to the biggest office gossip, Kelly, and he says Stanley's having an affair.
他跑去找办公室最大的八卦精凯莉，告诉她斯坦利有外遇。

927
00:42:22.880 --> 00:42:23.940
She's like, what?
她反应是，什么？

928
00:42:24.160 --> 00:42:27.640
We had a fan catch from Sarah G in Ottawa.
我们收到了一位来自渥太华的粉丝莎拉·G的发现。

929
00:42:28.540 --> 00:42:36.620
At around 6 minutes 30 seconds, when Michael tells Kelly about Stanley's affair, there's a whiteboard behind her desk that reads people's names and numbers.
在大约6分30秒时，当迈克尔告诉凯莉关于斯坦利外遇的事，她桌子后面有个白板，上面写着人的名字和数字。

930
00:42:36.620 --> 00:42:41.640
It says sales, quarterly sales, and HR performance.
上面写着销售额、季度销售额和人力资源绩效。

931
00:42:43.260 --> 00:42:49.740
Sarah notes, one, Pam is not on there, even though she is a salesperson now, but Creed is.
莎拉指出，第一，帕姆不在上面，尽管她现在是销售员，但克里德却在上面。

932
00:42:50.020 --> 00:42:51.820
Sarah wants to know why is that?
莎拉想知道这是为什么？

933
00:42:52.600 --> 00:42:57.220
Sarah, I do not think that this whiteboard has been changed in like two seasons.
莎拉，我觉得这个白板大概有两个季度没换过了。

934
00:42:57.460 --> 00:42:58.200
For sure.
肯定的。

935
00:42:58.360 --> 00:43:01.320
Because I remember seeing this whiteboard in season three.
