1093
00:50:07.360 --> 00:50:11.120
Well, Randy told me that this was a trick.
兰迪告诉我这其实是个小把戏。

1094
00:50:11.340 --> 00:50:12.080
There's nothing there.
那里什么都没有。

1095
00:50:12.360 --> 00:50:12.920
Fakie tree?
假树？

1096
00:50:13.180 --> 00:50:13.960
Fakie tree.
假树。

1097
00:50:14.300 --> 00:50:14.920
Yes.
是的。

1098
00:50:15.900 --> 00:50:25.600
They took a leafy branch, and they put it on a grip stand, and then someone would shake it a little bit to make it seem like there was a breeze.
他们拿了一根带叶子的树枝，把它放在灯架上，然后有人会轻轻晃动它，让它看起来像是有微风吹过。

1099
00:50:25.860 --> 00:50:32.060
And Matt composed his shot to include some of those leaves so that it would look like a spy shot.
马特在构图时把那些叶子也拍了进去，这样看起来就像是偷拍镜头。

1100
00:50:32.060 --> 00:50:38.980
Why in my brain do I hear someone like on a walkie-talkie going, too much movement.
为什么我脑子里总能听到有人在对讲机里说，动作幅度太大了。

1101
00:50:39.120 --> 00:50:39.740
Too much shaking.
晃得太厉害了。

1102
00:50:40.500 --> 00:50:41.640
Shake it up higher.
往高处晃。

1103
00:50:42.220 --> 00:50:42.600
Shake it.
晃一晃。

1104
00:50:42.660 --> 00:50:43.280
Shake it lower.
往低处晃。

1105
00:50:44.400 --> 00:50:50.140
Now, I don't know if Randy was teasing me, but he told me the technical term for this is called a brancholaurus.
我不知道兰迪是不是在逗我，但他告诉我这个术语叫“分支龙”。

1106
00:50:50.540 --> 00:50:51.220
Come on.
得了吧。

1107
00:50:51.360 --> 00:50:53.920
He said it's often used in outdoor shooting.
他说这通常用于户外拍摄。

1108
00:50:54.180 --> 00:50:54.740
Come on.
得了吧。

1109
00:50:54.760 --> 00:50:55.400
Is that true?
那是真的吗？

1110
00:50:55.520 --> 00:50:56.080
I don't know.
我不知道。

1111
00:50:56.240 --> 00:50:57.660
Randy, a brancholaurus.
兰迪，分支龙。

1112
00:50:57.660 --> 00:50:59.720
Is he listening to our podcast?
他在听我们的播客吗？

1113
00:50:59.840 --> 00:51:01.320
He's like, they bought it.
他肯定在想，他们居然信了。

1114
00:51:02.540 --> 00:51:03.020
Brancholaurus.
分支龙。

1115
00:51:03.540 --> 00:51:04.780
That's so fun.
太好玩了。

1116
00:51:04.940 --> 00:51:10.900
If I'm ever directing Randy and I call for a brancholaurus and people don't know what I'm talking about, I'm calling you.
如果以后我执导兰迪的戏，我喊“分支龙”而别人听不懂的话，我就找你。

1117
00:51:11.940 --> 00:51:16.980
Well, Michael is going to promise Stanley that he won't say anything, but we already know it's too late for that.
迈克尔打算向斯坦利保证他什么都不会说，但我们都知道已经太晚了。

1118
00:51:17.220 --> 00:51:26.060
So now he comes up with this crazy idea that what he has to do is diffuse that one piece of information by just throwing out all kinds of rumors.
所以他想出了个疯狂的主意，打算通过散布各种谣言来冲淡那条消息。

1119
00:51:26.340 --> 00:51:26.760
Yeah.
没错。

1120
00:51:26.760 --> 00:51:30.500
He finds Kevin in the kitchen making cookies?
他发现凯文在厨房烤饼干？

1121
00:51:30.960 --> 00:51:33.660
Yeah, he's making cookies in the toaster oven.
对，他在小烤箱里烤饼干。

1122
00:51:33.760 --> 00:51:34.100
Mm-hmm.
嗯。

1123
00:51:34.820 --> 00:51:40.360
Michael says, have you heard about Angela dating an 81-year-old billionaire who owns a Quiznos?
迈克尔说，你听说安吉拉在和一个拥有Quiznos连锁店的81岁亿万富翁约会吗？

1124
00:51:40.820 --> 00:51:45.400
Then he goes up to reception and he tells Aaron that Kelly is an anorexetic.
然后他走到前台，告诉亚伦说凯莉患有厌食症。

1125
00:51:45.700 --> 00:51:54.160
Did you notice at 10 minutes, 25 seconds that Aaron's little desk area has a Keystone College little banner?
你有没有注意到在10分25秒的时候，亚伦的小办公桌区域有个基斯通学院的小横幅？

1126
00:51:54.400 --> 00:51:54.800
Yes.
注意到了。

1127
00:51:54.800 --> 00:51:57.160
And a teddy bear with a red hoodie.
还有一个穿着红色连帽衫的泰迪熊。

1128
00:51:57.360 --> 00:52:00.060
I got real interested in her reception desk, Angela.
安吉拉，我对她的前台桌子非常感兴趣。

1129
00:52:00.200 --> 00:52:01.200
Oh, did you?
哦，是吗？

1130
00:52:01.200 --> 00:52:07.840
You and I obviously were thinking the same thing because when I saw that Keystone College banner, I was like, hold up.
显然我们想到一块去了，因为当我看到那个基斯通学院的横幅时，我就想，等等。

1131
00:52:07.840 --> 00:52:10.680
I want to know more about Aaron.
我想更多地了解亚伦。

1132
00:52:10.940 --> 00:52:12.220
What will her desk reveal?
她的桌子会透露出什么呢？

1133
00:52:12.220 --> 00:52:13.460
What did you find?
你发现了什么？

1134
00:52:13.780 --> 00:52:18.400
Well, Keystone College is a real private college in Northwestern Pennsylvania.
基斯通学院是宾夕法尼亚州西北部的一所真实私立学院。

1135
00:52:19.000 --> 00:52:24.300
And not only does she have a stuffed dog with a little sweater, that little sweater says J-Rob.
而且她不仅有一个穿着小毛衣的毛绒狗，那件小毛衣上还写着“J-Rob”。

1136
00:52:24.720 --> 00:52:30.800
And then she has a pink ski boot mug that she has put her pens and pencils in.
然后她还有一个粉色的滑雪靴形状的马克杯，用来装她的钢笔和铅笔。

1137
00:52:30.800 --> 00:52:33.340
And that also says J-Rob.
上面也写着“J-Rob”。

1138
00:52:33.740 --> 00:52:35.080
What is J-Rob?
J-Rob是什么？

1139
00:52:35.660 --> 00:52:36.920
I Googled it.
我谷歌了一下。

1140
00:52:37.080 --> 00:52:39.820
And it is a wrestling camp in Pennsylvania.
那是宾夕法尼亚州的一个摔跤训练营。

1141
00:52:40.160 --> 00:52:40.740
Get out.
别开玩笑了。

1142
00:52:41.060 --> 00:52:42.980
I don't think this is correct.
我觉得这不对。

1143
00:52:43.300 --> 00:52:45.300
Why they would sell a ski boot.
他们为什么要卖滑雪靴呢？

1144
00:52:45.360 --> 00:52:48.160
I looked at all their merch for this wrestling camp.
我看了那个摔跤训练营所有的周边商品。

1145
00:52:48.360 --> 00:52:50.400
I don't even think the logo is the same.
我觉得连标志都不一样。

1146
00:52:50.640 --> 00:52:52.340
Did Aaron go to wrestling camp?
亚伦去过摔跤训练营吗？

1147
00:52:52.340 --> 00:52:54.100
I am very stumped on this one.
这个问题真把我难住了。

1148
00:52:54.220 --> 00:52:55.060
I don't know.
我不知道。

1149
00:52:55.260 --> 00:52:59.600
But Aaron also has a candy dish with some individually wrapped Lifesavers in it.
但亚伦桌上还有一个糖果盘，里面装了一些独立包装的救生圈糖。

1150
00:52:59.920 --> 00:53:01.240
Phil Shea, what is J-Rob?
菲尔·谢，J-Rob到底是什么？

1151
00:53:01.500 --> 00:53:02.780
What is J-Rob?
J-Rob是什么？

1152
00:53:02.980 --> 00:53:05.360
And then I was like, is it J-R-B-B?
然后我就在想，是J-R-B-B吗？

1153
00:53:05.580 --> 00:53:07.260
Like J-R-B-B?
就像J-R-B-B那样？

1154
00:53:07.520 --> 00:53:09.260
Or is it J-R-O-B?
还是J-R-O-B？

1155
00:53:09.980 --> 00:53:11.380
I Googled both.
我两个都搜了。

1156
00:53:11.560 --> 00:53:15.020
But there is a wrestling camp in Pennsylvania called J-Rob.
结果宾夕法尼亚州有个摔跤训练营叫J-Rob。

1157
00:53:15.260 --> 00:53:15.620
Okay.
好吧。

1158
00:53:16.600 --> 00:53:18.640
Michael's going to continue his rumor mill.
迈克尔要继续他的造谣工厂了。

1159
00:53:18.640 --> 00:53:23.480
He's going to tell Kelly that Aaron isn't a very good worker and may not last long at
他要告诉凯利，亚伦工作表现不好，可能在邓德 Mifflin公司干不长了，

1160
00:53:23.480 --> 00:53:25.420
Dundra Mifflin and that Andy is gay.
还说安迪是同性恋。

1161
00:53:25.620 --> 00:53:27.580
He tells Meredith that Pam is pregnant.
他告诉梅雷迪思说帕姆怀孕了。

1162
00:53:28.100 --> 00:53:30.560
So he's really throwing a lot of stuff out there.
所以他真的是到处散布各种消息。

1163
00:53:30.720 --> 00:53:33.880
Of course, we know, oh my gosh, Pam is pregnant.
当然，我们都知道，天哪，帕姆确实怀孕了。

1164
00:53:34.200 --> 00:53:34.680
Yeah.
没错。

1165
00:53:35.040 --> 00:53:38.780
Well, now the rumors are just traveling all crazy throughout the office.
现在这些谣言在办公室里传得乱七八糟的。

1166
00:53:39.000 --> 00:53:39.340
Yes.
是的。

1167
00:53:39.460 --> 00:53:42.720
And now people are going to start hearing the rumors about themselves.
现在大家开始听到关于自己的谣言了。

1168
00:53:43.080 --> 00:53:43.300
Yeah.
没错。

1169
00:53:43.560 --> 00:53:46.100
Andy hears this rumor that he might be gay.
安迪听到了关于他可能是同性恋的传闻。

1170
00:53:46.280 --> 00:53:46.980
From Kevin.
是从凯文那听来的。

1171
00:53:47.120 --> 00:53:48.260
And he's like, was this Broccoli Rob?
他就在想，是西兰花罗伯说的吗？

1172
00:53:48.640 --> 00:53:49.060
Yes.
是的。

1173
00:53:49.240 --> 00:53:50.200
Was it someone in high school?
还是高中里的某个人？

1174
00:53:50.400 --> 00:53:53.240
This sends Andy on an existential crisis.
这让安迪陷入了存在主义危机。

1175
00:53:53.860 --> 00:53:56.800
And he's going to confront Oscar in the break room.
他准备去休息室找奥斯卡对质。

1176
00:53:57.000 --> 00:53:58.840
Oscar has such a great talking head.
奥斯卡的个人采访片段太棒了。

1177
00:53:59.020 --> 00:54:01.080
After that scene with Andy where he's like,
在安迪那场戏之后，他说，

1178
00:54:01.700 --> 00:54:05.060
what, it's my responsibility to comfort the insecure heterosexual men?
什么，难道安慰那些缺乏安全感的异性恋男人是我的责任吗？

1179
00:54:05.240 --> 00:54:06.780
That can't possibly fall on me.
这怎么可能落到我头上。

1180
00:54:07.200 --> 00:54:09.460
I'm paraphrasing it, but it's something like that.
我这是意译，但大概就是这个意思。

1181
00:54:09.520 --> 00:54:10.160
It's so good.
太精彩了。

1182
00:54:10.440 --> 00:54:16.660
When Andy is describing this scenario where Brad Pitt is like coming on to him.
当安迪描述那个布拉德·皮特对他示好的场景时。

1183
00:54:16.720 --> 00:54:18.000
At like a beach cabana.
就在海滩小屋那边。

1184
00:54:18.000 --> 00:54:23.380
Yes, and Brad Pitt is trying to kiss him and Andy resists, but Brad Pitt keeps coming for him.
是的，布拉德·皮特想亲他，安迪拒绝了，但布拉德·皮特还是不依不饶。

1185
00:54:23.900 --> 00:54:32.140
Oscar has this amazing line where he says, so if you resisted Brad Pitt a little bit, he would still need to get to you.
奥斯卡说了句绝妙的台词，他说，所以如果你稍微反抗一下布拉德·皮特，他还是会想方设法得到你。

1186
00:54:34.580 --> 00:54:43.740
Lady, the mention of Brad Pitt made me very randomly think about how I have had recurring dreams about Brad Pitt making me soup.
女士，提到布拉德·皮特让我突然想到，我经常梦见布拉德·皮特给我做汤。

1187
00:54:43.740 --> 00:54:44.320
What?
什么？

1188
00:54:44.600 --> 00:54:46.000
He makes me soup.
他给我做汤。

1189
00:54:46.160 --> 00:54:47.280
What does this mean?
这代表什么？

1190
00:54:48.980 --> 00:54:49.840
Recurring dream.
反复出现的梦。

1191
00:54:50.060 --> 00:54:51.180
Like over your life?
是贯穿你整个人生吗？

1192
00:54:51.320 --> 00:54:51.700
Yes.
是的。

1193
00:54:51.880 --> 00:54:53.380
Like since college.
从大学开始就这样。

1194
00:54:53.660 --> 00:54:54.160
What?
什么？

1195
00:54:54.700 --> 00:54:58.880
And Brad Pitt would make me a warm, comforting bowl of soup.
布拉德·皮特会给我做一碗温暖、治愈的汤。

1196
00:54:58.960 --> 00:55:00.540
And it would make me happy.
这让我感到很幸福。

1197
00:55:00.540 --> 00:55:02.740
And he was my friend in my dreaMs.
在梦里他是我的朋友。

1198
00:55:02.900 --> 00:55:03.900
Was he fully clothed?
他穿衣服了吗？

1199
00:55:03.900 --> 00:55:04.440
Yes.
穿了。

1200
00:55:04.900 --> 00:55:07.240
It was just a wonderful gesture.
那只是一个非常美好的举动。

1201
00:55:07.640 --> 00:55:12.880
So I looked up, you know, dreams and meaning of dreaMs.
所以我查了查，你知道，关于梦和梦的含义。

1202
00:55:13.100 --> 00:55:14.980
What does it mean if you have soup in your dream?
梦见喝汤是什么意思？

1203
00:55:15.140 --> 00:55:21.020
Well, what a celebrity in your dream is, is that the celebrity is you.
嗯，梦里的名人其实就是你自己。

1204
00:55:21.300 --> 00:55:23.760
It's like a version of you.
就像是另一个版本的你。

1205
00:55:24.060 --> 00:55:27.060
So you are Brad Pitt and you're making yourself soup?
所以你是布拉德·皮特，然后你在给自己做汤？

1206
00:55:27.240 --> 00:55:28.200
I guess so.
我想是吧。

1207
00:55:28.200 --> 00:55:31.920
But more than that, here's what I determined it to be.
但不仅如此，我得出了这样的结论。

1208
00:55:32.620 --> 00:55:34.180
Brad Pitt is from Missouri.
布拉德·皮特来自密苏里州。

1209
00:55:34.900 --> 00:55:36.500
He's from where I grew up.
他来自我长大的地方。

1210
00:55:36.700 --> 00:55:38.020
So I think.
所以我想。

1211
00:55:38.160 --> 00:55:40.820
He was the big local celebrity when you were growing up.
他是我成长过程中当地的大名人。

1212
00:55:41.000 --> 00:55:46.260
He went to Mizzou, which was the college about an hour and a half away from my college.
他去了密苏里大学，那所大学离我的大学大约一个半小时的路程。

1213
00:55:46.440 --> 00:55:47.400
He didn't finish.
他没读完。

1214
00:55:47.720 --> 00:55:50.160
But then he went off and he became a big star.
但他后来离开了，成了一位大明星。

1215
00:55:50.620 --> 00:55:52.020
You know, I've never met him.
你知道，我从来没见过他。

1216
00:55:52.100 --> 00:55:55.340
I've never been able to geek out with him about our Missouri roots.
我从来没机会和他一起兴奋地聊聊我们的密苏里渊源。

1217
00:55:55.700 --> 00:55:57.040
But it was a big deal.
但这确实是一件大事。

1218
00:55:57.040 --> 00:56:01.040
Like when you're from Missouri and someone else from Missouri is super famous, like everybody
就像当你来自密苏里州，而另一个来自密苏里州的人变得超级有名时，每个人

1219
00:56:01.040 --> 00:56:01.960
knows it, you know?
都知道，你懂吗？

1220
00:56:02.480 --> 00:56:04.960
Oh, man, I can never meet him now.
天哪，我现在永远没法见他了。

1221
00:56:05.320 --> 00:56:05.760
Why?
为什么？

1222
00:56:06.040 --> 00:56:07.800
Because I know me.
因为我了解我自己。

1223
00:56:08.000 --> 00:56:08.920
You're going to say something.
你肯定会说些什么的。

1224
00:56:08.940 --> 00:56:12.660
And I know if I meet Brad Pitt, I won't be able to.
我知道如果我见到布拉德·皮特，我肯定会控制不住。

1225
00:56:12.840 --> 00:56:14.340
It'll be like a Michael Scott moment.
那会像迈克尔·斯科特时刻一样尴尬。

1226
00:56:14.340 --> 00:56:18.160
I'll say, my friend Jenna dreams that you make her soup.
我会说，我朋友珍娜梦见你给她做汤。

1227
00:56:19.960 --> 00:56:21.720
It'll just come tumbling out.
话就会脱口而出。

1228
00:56:22.000 --> 00:56:23.500
I can never meet him.
我永远没法见他了。

1229
00:56:23.700 --> 00:56:25.720
How can I ever meet him now?
我现在怎么可能见他呢？

1230
00:56:25.720 --> 00:56:30.600
When I know that my best friend since college has dreamed that he makes her soup.
当我明知我大学以来的好朋友梦见他给她做汤的时候。

1231
00:56:31.260 --> 00:56:32.640
Here's what I think it is.
我是这么想的。

1232
00:56:32.800 --> 00:56:40.960
I think he represents like whenever I felt homesick, I'll have a dream where like my hometown is
我觉得他代表了每当我感到想家时，我就会做一个梦，梦见我的家乡

1233
00:56:40.960 --> 00:56:41.960
making me soup.
在给我做汤。

1234
00:56:42.160 --> 00:56:43.580
Like that's what I think it is.
我觉得就是这样。

1235
00:56:43.640 --> 00:56:45.740
I think it's like a homesickness dream.
我觉得这是一种思乡梦。

1236
00:56:45.740 --> 00:56:49.020
I have never had a dream about Brad Pitt.
我从来没梦见过布拉德·皮特。

1237
00:56:49.280 --> 00:56:50.900
Well, his soup is delicious.
嗯，他做的汤很美味。

1238
00:56:51.020 --> 00:56:55.060
I just want to say it's homemade and it's very, very good.
我只想说那是家常口味，而且非常好喝。

1239
00:56:55.220 --> 00:56:56.980
And it's always the soup is different.
而且每次的汤都不一样。

1240
00:56:57.280 --> 00:57:02.020
It's been I remember very distinctly there was a vegetable and another time a cream of
我记得很清楚，有一次是蔬菜汤，还有一次是奶油

1241
00:57:02.020 --> 00:57:02.340
potato.
土豆汤。

1242
00:57:02.900 --> 00:57:07.780
I had a dream after I saw the matrix that I could, you know, that I was like a badass
看完《黑客帝国》后，我做了一个梦，梦见我，你知道，我像基努一样

1243
00:57:07.780 --> 00:57:11.400
with Keanu and I was like, I could do all that stuff.
是个狠角色，我当时觉得，我能做所有那些事。

